1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,747
This town loses gravity for one minute every day.

2
00:00:02,827 --> 00:00:04,580
At exactly twelve o'clock.

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:05,813
A siren goes off,

4
00:00:05,893 --> 00:00:08,113
and everyone grabs the nearest railing.

5
00:00:08,193 --> 00:00:09,647
Because if you don't... you float.

6
00:00:09,727 --> 00:00:10,685
Cars float.

7
00:00:10,827 --> 00:00:11,788
Dogs float.

8
00:00:11,927 --> 00:00:13,780
Even the mayor's toupee floats.

9
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,162
Sixty seconds later, everything drops.

10
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,780
We call it Float Hour. Even though it's a minute.

11
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:19,766
I'm Ivy.

12
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,613
This is my little brother, Bo.

13
00:00:21,693 --> 00:00:23,947
Bo has never held a railing in his life.

14
00:00:24,027 --> 00:00:26,313
He says floating is the best part of the day.

15
00:00:26,393 --> 00:00:29,847
Our grandpa Gus winds the giant town clock every morning.

16
00:00:29,927 --> 00:00:31,347
He told us one rule.

17
00:00:31,427 --> 00:00:32,913
"If the clock ever stops...

18
00:00:32,993 --> 00:00:34,765
hold on, and don't let go."

19
00:00:34,927 --> 00:00:35,747
Bo laughed.

20
00:00:36,027 --> 00:00:37,347
Then came Tuesday.

21
00:00:37,427 --> 00:00:39,556
11:59. The siren.

22
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,247
Everyone grabbed a railing.

23
00:00:41,327 --> 00:00:42,847
Bo grabbed his balloon.

24
00:00:42,927 --> 00:00:44,880
Twelve o'clock. We floated.

25
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:47,213
Ten seconds. Thirty. Sixty.

26
00:00:47,293 --> 00:00:48,580
Nothing came down.

27
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:49,947
The clock had stopped.

28
00:00:50,027 --> 00:00:51,780
And everything kept going up.

29
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,690
Cars. Mailboxes. The school bus.

30
00:00:54,793 --> 00:00:57,247
The fountain water floated up in giant bubbles.

31
00:00:57,327 --> 00:00:59,347
Bo waved at me... and kept rising.

32
00:00:59,427 --> 00:01:00,913
I screamed his name.

33
00:01:00,993 --> 00:01:04,180
Grandpa yelled, "The key! Someone stole the key!"

34
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:06,667
Without the key, the clock can't be wound.

35
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:09,547
And without the clock, there's no gravity at all.

36
00:01:09,627 --> 00:01:11,847
The whole town was drifting into the clouds.

37
00:01:11,927 --> 00:01:13,247
That's when I saw him.

38
00:01:13,327 --> 00:01:15,456
Mayor Grimsby. Holding the key.

39
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:17,380
"No more Float Hour," he said.

40
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,113
"From now on... it's Float Forever!"

41
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:21,580
His new sky hotel opens tomorrow.

42
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:22,713
So I let go.

43
00:01:22,793 --> 00:01:25,480
I pushed off a lamppost and flew straight at him.

44
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,780
Biscuit flew with me.

45
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,280
Biscuit bit the toupee.

46
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,813
The mayor dropped the key.

47
00:01:29,893 --> 00:01:30,730
I caught it.

48
00:01:30,993 --> 00:01:32,747
Gravity: three percent.

49
00:01:32,827 --> 00:01:34,913
I grabbed Bo's shoelace on the way up.

50
00:01:34,993 --> 00:01:37,180
Grandpa held the clock door open.

51
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:38,947
The keyhole was taller than me.

52
00:01:39,027 --> 00:01:42,113
We all pushed. Once. Twice. Three times.

53
00:01:42,193 --> 00:01:43,880
The gears roared back to life.

54
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:44,512
Tick.

55
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:47,713
Everything came down. Really fast.

56
00:01:47,793 --> 00:01:49,447
The mayor landed in the fountain.

57
00:01:49,527 --> 00:01:51,347
His toupee landed on Biscuit.

58
00:01:51,427 --> 00:01:53,313
Biscuit refuses to give it back.

59
00:01:53,393 --> 00:01:55,947
Now the key hangs around Grandpa's neck.

60
00:01:56,027 --> 00:01:58,310
The mayor? He polishes railings now.

61
00:01:58,393 --> 00:02:00,498
And Bo holds a railing. Mostly.

62
00:02:00,593 --> 00:02:02,180
Everything was normal again.

63
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:04,747
But last night, I woke up at 3 a.m.

64
00:02:04,827 --> 00:02:06,580
My bed was touching the ceiling.

65
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,813
And the clock tower said twelve o'clock.

66
00:02:08,893 --> 00:02:10,280
Someone else has a key.

67
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,239
Hold on.

